    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully tested. The API survived the restart with click counts intact, migrations are idempotent, and the server is stopped with port 8000 freed.\n\nWhat I built:\n\n- **Stack**: Express pinned to exactly 4.21.2, with Knex + `pg` as the idiomatic persistence layer. Connection comes solely from `DATABASE_URL` (knexfile throws if unset).\n- **Migration**: `migrations/20240101000000_create_links.js` creates `links` (auto `id`, unique `code` up to 20 chars, `url` text, `clicks` int default 0, `created_at`).\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201, duplicate custom code → 409, bad url/code → 422, auto-generated 8-char codes with collision retry), `GET /links/:code` (200/404), `GET /r/:code` (302 with atomic `clicks + 1` via a single `UPDATE ... RETURNING`, unknown → 404 without incrementing), and `GET /links` (id-ascending items + total). Malformed JSON bodies are caught by an error handler and mapped to 422.\n- **`start.sh`**: applies pending migrations with `npx knex migrate:latest`, then `exec node src/server.js` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; no installs inside the script. README documents startup.\n\nAll 13 curl scenarios passed, including boundary code lengths (4/20 chars), `ftp://` and hostless URLs rejected, and clicks incrementing exactly once per redirect."
